{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And the Levites shall answer.</b> Meaning — and they shall begin: they will begin to speak and the people will answer after them, אָמֵן. And Onkelos translated ״וְיָתִיבוּן״, and according to his words, ״וְעָנוּ הַלְוִיִּם״ is an answer for standing Israel in this arrangement on the mountains, which is to make them hear the statements uttered from their mouths — ״בָּרוּךְ אֲשֶׁר״ etc. and ״אָרוּר אֲשֶׁר״. And Jonathan translated ״וְיַכְרְזוּן לֵוָאֵי״, and it is difficult for me, for behold it says ״קוֹל רָם״. But perhaps the proclamation would be by voice, aside from the raising of the voice in the utterance itself."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:19:16.317892630Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}